 Workarounds
 ===========
 
+KK_WORKAROUND_15
+----------------
+| macOS version: 26.x
+| Metal ticket: Not reported
+| Metal ticket status:
+| CTS test failure: ``dEQP-GL45-ES31.functional.shaders.opaque_type_indexing.sampler.*.tessellation_evaluation.*``
+| Comments:
+
+Large compute kernels miscompile when a global access is marked ``coherent``:
+part way through the kernel every ``device`` load starts returning zero, and
+the point at which that begins moves earlier as the thread index grows. The
+zeroed loads include descriptor-set reads, so sampler and buffer descriptors
+collapse to zero and the affected invocations sample the wrong texture or skip
+their stores entirely. The memory being read is intact when the host inspects
+it after the submission, and ``volatile`` reproduces the same failure, so the
+trigger is the re-issued load rather than the coherency qualifier itself.
+
+Emulated tessellation evaluation, geometry and transform feedback stages re-run
+the application shader as a compute kernel and are large enough to hit this.
+KK_WORKAROUND_6 marked every global access ``coherent``, which is what makes
+those kernels re-issue their loads.
+
+Restrict KK_WORKAROUND_6 to accesses inside a loop, which is where the memory
+coherency issue it works around can actually be observed. Loop-free kernels
+keep ordinary ``device`` accesses and compile correctly. Disabling this
+workaround restores the unconditional ``coherent`` marking.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-09-07: Workaround implemented
+
 KK_WORKAROUND_14
 ----------------
 | macOS version: 26.5, 27.0 beta 1
@@ -250,6 +280,7 @@ Hopefully this does not affect performance much.
 | Log:
 | 2025-12-08: Workaround implemented and reported to Apple
 | 2026-06-22: Fixed in macOS 27 Beta (Build 26A5353q)
+| 2026-09-07: Restricted to accesses inside a loop, see KK_WORKAROUND_15
 
 KK_WORKAROUND_5
 ---------------
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
index 76b3cc9740463a32d5b4dc1ebad096a7bc09fc05..318a0cbd32a608cab739ff7ebc066b1b1c052af3 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/compiler/nir_to_msl.c
@@ -246,6 +246,32 @@ output_type(nir_shader *shader)
    }
 }
 
+/* KK_WORKAROUND_6, KK_WORKAROUND_15 */
+static bool
+msl_instr_in_loop(const nir_instr *instr)
+{
+   for (const nir_cf_node *n = &instr->block->cf_node; n; n = n->parent) {
+      if (n->type == nir_cf_node_loop)
+         return true;
+   }
+
+   return false;
+}
+
+static bool
+msl_coherent_workaround(const struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx,
+                        const nir_instr *instr)
+{
+   if (ctx->disabled_workarounds & BITFIELD64_BIT(6))
+      return false;
+
+   /* KK_WORKAROUND_15 */
+   if (ctx->disabled_workarounds & BITFIELD64_BIT(15))
+      return true;
+
+   return msl_instr_in_loop(instr);
+}
+
 static void
 emit_local_vars(struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx, nir_shader *shader)
 {
@@ -1456,8 +1482,8 @@ intrinsic_to_msl(struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx, nir_intrinsic_instr *instr)
    case nir_intrinsic_load_global: {
       enum gl_access_qualifier access = nir_intrinsic_access(instr);
       const char *type = msl_type_for_def(ctx->types, &instr->def);
-      const bool apply_workaround =
-         !(ctx->disabled_workarounds & BITFIELD64_BIT(6));
+      /* KK_WORKAROUND_6 */
+      const bool apply_workaround = msl_coherent_workaround(ctx, &instr->instr);
       const char *addressing = apply_workaround || (access & ACCESS_COHERENT)
                                   ? "coherent device"
                                   : "device";
@@ -1529,8 +1555,8 @@ intrinsic_to_msl(struct nir_to_msl_ctx *ctx, nir_intrinsic_instr *instr)
    case nir_intrinsic_store_global: {
       enum gl_access_qualifier access = nir_intrinsic_access(instr);
       const char *type = msl_type_for_src(ctx->types, &instr->src[0]);
-      const bool apply_workaround =
-         !(ctx->disabled_workarounds & BITFIELD64_BIT(6));
+      /* KK_WORKAROUND_6 */
+      const bool apply_workaround = msl_coherent_workaround(ctx, &instr->instr);
       const char *addressing = apply_workaround || (access & ACCESS_COHERENT)
                                   ? "coherent device"
                                   : "device";
